const faqItems = [
  { question: "Are edibles legal in Maine?", answer: "Yes. Cannabis edibles are legal in Maine for adults 21 and older, sold only through state-licensed adult-use dispensaries and registered medical dispensaries. The Maine Office of Cannabis Policy (OCP) regulates edibles under Title 28-B of the Maine Revised Statutes. You must show a valid government-issued photo ID proving you are 21+ to buy them." },
  { question: "Where can I legally buy edibles in Maine?", answer: "Only at a licensed Maine adult-use dispensary or a registered medical dispensary. Edibles sold at gas stations, convenience stores, smoke shops, or online are not part of the regulated program and are illegal in Maine. As of the OCP 2025 annual report, Maine has roughly 180 active adult-use retail stores across 78 retail-authorized municipalities." },
  { question: "What is the THC limit on Maine edibles?", answer: "Maine caps a single serving at 10mg of THC and a single package at 200mg of THC, with a 10% allowable variance per Title 28-B §703(1)(F). A standard 10mg gummy can be split in half for a 5mg starting dose." },
  { question: "Do I need a medical card to buy edibles in Maine?", answer: "No. Adults 21+ can buy adult-use edibles with just a valid photo ID, no medical card required. A Maine medical cannabis card (or a valid out-of-state card from a reciprocity state) lets you buy at medical dispensaries, which may carry higher-dose products than the 200mg adult-use package ceiling." },
  { question: "Are hemp-derived THC gummies from a smoke shop legal in Maine?", answer: "No. Hemp-derived THC products sold outside the licensed dispensary system are not regulated by the OCP, are not METRC-tracked, and have been the subject of OCP and Department of Agriculture enforcement actions in 2024-2026. Their labeling is unreliable and they are illegal in Maine regardless of packaging claims." },
  { question: "Can I make edibles at home to sell in Maine?", answer: "No. Commercial edibles must be produced in a licensed Products Manufacturing facility that meets OCP food-safety standards. Home kitchens do not qualify. Selling homemade edibles is illegal. For the full operator rules, see the Maine cannabis edibles compliance guide." },
  { question: "Can I consume edibles in public in Maine?", answer: "No. Maine law prohibits public consumption of cannabis, including edibles. Consume only on private property with the owner's consent. Cannabis remains illegal on all federal land, including Acadia National Park." },
  { question: "How much does a Maine edible cost?", answer: "A single 10mg gummy typically runs $3-6, and a 100mg multi-serving package runs $20-35 depending on the operator and format. Prices vary by brand, potency, and whether the product uses full-spectrum distillate or RSO versus bulk distillate." }
];

